{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":9833385,"ns":0,"title":"Butt welding","extract":"Butt welding is when two pieces of metal are placed end-to-end without overlap and then welded along the joint (as opposed to lap joint weld, where one piece of metal is laid on top of the other, or plug welding, where one piece of metal is inserted into the other). Importantly, in a butt joint, the surfaces of the workpieces being joined are on the same plane and the weld metal remains within the planes of the surfaces.","description":"Welding of metal pieces placed end-to-end (butt joint)","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}